---
// GuideSection.astro — 600-word SEO educational guide
---

<section
  id="guide"
  style="
  padding: 96px 24px;
  background: transparent;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--border-hairline);
"
>
  <div style="max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto;">
    <!-- Section eyebrow -->
    <p
      style="
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 12px;
      font-weight: 600;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.12em;
      color: #F59E0B;
      margin: 0 0 16px;
    "
    >
      Platform Guide
    </p>

    <h2
      style="
      font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 38px);
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: -1.2px;
      color: var(--text-ink);
      margin: 0 0 40px;
      line-height: 1.15;
    "
    >
      Understanding digital platform fees: a guide for creators.
    </h2>

    <div
      style="
      font-size: 16px;
      line-height: 1.75;
      color: var(--text-body);
    "
      class="guide-content"
    >
      <h3
        style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-ink); margin: 0 0 12px; letter-spacing: -0.4px;"
      >
        How platform fees actually work
      </h3>
      <p style="margin: 0 0 24px;">
        Every platform that sells digital products — whether an ebook, template,
        course, or SaaS subscription — charges some combination of a <strong
          style="color: var(--text-ink);">platform percentage</strong
        >, a <strong style="color: var(--text-ink);"
          >fixed transaction fee</strong
        >, and a <strong style="color: var(--text-ink);"
          >payment processing fee</strong
        >. These three layers compound differently depending on your price
        point, which is why a platform that looks "cheaper" at $10 products can
        be more expensive at $100 products.
      </p>
      <p style="margin: 0 0 24px;">
        Take Gumroad's Direct pricing: 10% of the sale price plus $0.50 per
        transaction, plus approximately 2.9% + $0.30 for card processing. On a
        $5 digital download, Gumroad's effective take is over 25%. On a $100
        product, it drops to roughly 14%. This non-linear relationship is
        exactly why a static comparison table misleads creators — the "best"
        platform is always price-and-volume dependent.
      </p>

      <h3
        style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-ink); margin: 0 0 12px; letter-spacing: -0.4px;"
      >
        The hidden cost of fixed transaction fees on low-ticket items
      </h3>
      <p style="margin: 0 0 24px;">
        Fixed per-transaction fees like $0.30 (Stripe) or $0.50 (Lemon Squeezy,
        Gumroad) are disproportionately devastating at low price points. Selling
        a $1 digital product on Stripe costs $0.33 in fees before the product
        percentage — a 33% overhead from a single line item. At $5, that same
        $0.30 is 6%. At $25, it's 1.2%.
      </p>
      <p style="margin: 0 0 24px;">
        This is why pricing your digital products at $10+ is often more critical
        than which platform you choose. Creators selling low-ticket tripwire
        offers (under $5) should consider platforms that bundle processing into
        one flat percentage without fixed fees, or use platforms like Payhip's
        Pro plan ($99/month flat, 0% per transaction) at sufficient volume.
      </p>

      <h3
        style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-ink); margin: 0 0 12px; letter-spacing: -0.4px;"
      >
        What is a Merchant of Record (MoR)?
      </h3>
      <p style="margin: 0 0 24px;">
        A Merchant of Record is a platform that legally takes on the
        responsibility of selling your products to customers — including
        collecting, calculating, filing, and remitting sales tax, VAT, and GST
        across every jurisdiction. Lemon Squeezy is the clearest example in this
        comparison.
      </p>
      <p style="margin: 0 0 24px;">
        Without an MoR, you are responsible for EU VAT registration once you
        exceed thresholds (typically €10,000 in EU-wide digital sales), US state
        sales tax registration in nexus states, Australian GST, UK VAT, and
        dozens more. This isn't theoretical risk — platforms like Gumroad,
        Stripe, Payhip, and Whop leave tax compliance entirely to you as the
        seller.
      </p>
      <p style="margin: 0 0 24px;">
        Lemon Squeezy's 5% + $0.50 fee includes this MoR coverage globally. When
        you factor in the cost of an accountant, tax software like TaxJar or
        Quaderno ($19–$99/month), or the risk of non-compliance penalties, an
        MoR platform often represents real savings beyond its fee percentage —
        especially for creators selling to international audiences.
      </p>

      <h3
        style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-ink); margin: 0 0 16px; letter-spacing: -0.4px;"
      >
        Platform comparison: who is each platform best for?
      </h3>

      <div
        style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px; margin: 0 0 32px;"
      >
        {
          [
            {
              name: "Stripe Direct",
              icon: "/icons/stripe.svg",
              description:
                "Best for maximum margin on high-volume, higher-priced products when you already have tax infrastructure. Lowest fees (2.9% + $0.30), but you handle all compliance, customer support integrations, and storefront yourself.",
            },
            {
              name: "Lemon Squeezy",
              icon: "/icons/lemonsqueezy.svg",
              description:
                "Best for international creators, SaaS founders, and digital product sellers who want complete global VAT/GST compliance handled automatically. 5% + $0.50 per sale with full MoR tax remittance.",
            },
            {
              name: "Paddle",
              icon: "/icons/paddle.svg",
              description:
                "Best for SaaS and digital software products operating globally as a Merchant of Record. 5% + $0.50 flat per sale auto-handles international tax compliance and localized checkout currencies.",
            },
            {
              name: "Payhip Pro",
              icon: "/icons/payhip.svg",
              description:
                "Best for high-volume creators selling above $50 products. Features Free (5%), Plus ($29/mo + 2%), and Pro ($99/mo + 0%) plans, dropping your effective rate below Stripe at sufficient volume.",
            },
            {
              name: "Gumroad",
              icon: "/icons/gumroad.svg",
              description:
                "Best for creators leveraging an existing Gumroad audience. Direct mode charges 10% + $0.50, while Discover marketplace takes 30% cut for driving organic sales.",
            },
            {
              name: "Whop",
              icon: "/icons/whop.svg",
              description:
                "Best for community products, Discord memberships, trading groups, and SaaS apps. Features a competitive 3% platform fee plus card processing (2.9% + $0.30).",
            },
            {
              name: "Sellfy",
              icon: "/icons/sellfy.svg",
              description:
                "Best for digital storefronts and merchandise. Starter plan ($29/mo) eliminates platform fees (0%) with direct payment gateway processing (2.9% + $0.30).",
            },
            {
              name: "Podia",
              icon: "/icons/podia.svg",
              description:
                "Best for creators selling online courses, digital downloads, and coaching. Mover plan ($39/mo) offers 0% transaction fees with standard card processing.",
            },
            {
              name: "Stan Store",
              icon: "/icons/stan.svg",
              description:
                "Best for social media creators and link-in-bio storefronts. Flat $29/mo plan with 0% platform transaction fee and direct card processing.",
            },
            {
              name: "Teachable",
              icon: "/icons/teachable.svg",
              description:
                "Best for structured course creators and academies. Basic ($39/mo + 5% fee) and Pro ($119/mo + 0% fee) allow creators to scale as student volume grows.",
            },
            {
              name: "Fiverr",
              icon: "/icons/fiverr.svg",
              description:
                "Best for freelancers, digital service providers, and gig creators selling packaged services or templates. Charges a flat 20% seller commission on all completed orders.",
            },
            {
              name: "Etsy",
              icon: "/icons/etsy.svg",
              description:
                "Best for digital downloads, creative templates, and printables targeting Etsy marketplace buyers. Charges $0.20 listing fee + 6.5% transaction fee + 3% + $0.25 payment processing.",
            },
            {
              name: "Amazon KDP",
              icon: "/icons/kdp.svg",
              description:
                "Best for self-published authors selling Kindle ebooks and digital books. Offers a 70% royalty tier (30% platform fee) plus an estimated $0.15/MB digital delivery fee.",
            },
            {
              name: "Upwork",
              icon: "/icons/upwork.svg",
              description:
                "Best for freelancers, consultants, and agencies working with global clients. Charges a flat 10% freelancer contract service fee.",
            },
          ].map(({ name, icon, description }) => (
            <div
              class="card-base"
              style="
              padding: 20px 24px;
              border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
              background: var(--bg-card);
              backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
              border: 1px solid var(--border-hairline);
            "
            >
              <p style="font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-ink); margin: 0 0 8px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px;">
                <img src={icon} width="20" height="20" alt={name} style="border-radius: 4px;" />
                {name}
              </p>
              <p style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-body); margin: 0; line-height: 1.6;">
                {description}
              </p>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>

      <h3
        style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-ink); margin: 0 0 12px; letter-spacing: -0.4px;"
      >
        International card surcharges and PayPal
      </h3>
      <p style="margin: 0 0 24px;">
        When customers use non-US credit or debit cards, Stripe applies a 1.5%
        international surcharge on top of the standard 2.9% rate. On platforms
        that pass card processing costs through (Gumroad Direct, Payhip, Whop),
        this surcharge flows to you. Use the "International Cards" toggle in the
        calculator above to model this scenario — particularly important if more
        than 30% of your audience is outside the United States.
      </p>
      <p style="margin: 0 0 0;">
        PayPal processing is an alternative to card processing on many
        platforms. PayPal's standard rate (3.49% + $0.49 per transaction) is
        typically more expensive than Stripe for small-ticket items but can be
        preferable for buyers who distrust card-on-file payments. Toggle PayPal
        in the calculator to compare the impact on your net margins.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
